{"schema_version":"1.0.0","id":"cik-0002023554","cik":"0002023554","slug":"sandisk-023554","name":"Sandisk Corp","ticker":"SNDK","exchanges":["Nasdaq"],"sector":"Computer Storage Devices","sic":"3572","country":"CA","website":"","listed_years":0.9,"first_annual":"2025-08-21","last_filing":"2026-07-02","annual_only":false,"edgar_url":"https://www.sec.gov/cgi-bin/browse-edgar?action=getcompany&CIK=0002023554&type=10-K","summary":{"sentences":["Sandisk Corp files with the SEC under \"Computer Storage Devices\", based in CA, and has been publicly reporting for 1 year.","It reported $13.0bn of revenue over the trailing four quarters, up 251.0% against the same quarter a year earlier, at a gross margin of 78.4%.","Listed on Nasdaq, it funds itself from operations ($357.0m of operating cash flow over the year)."],"generated":true,"note":"Assembled from filing metadata and XBRL figures. Not editorial judgement - and rule 7 asks whether *you* can explain it, so rewrite this in your own words before you rely on it."},"bull":[{"text":"Revenue grew 251.0% year on year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025), reaching $6.0bn in the quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Growth has been positive in 4 of the last 5 year-on-year comparisons, so this is a trend rather than one good quarter.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Gross margin of 78.4% means most of each additional sale falls through to cover fixed costs.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Gross margin expanded from 22.5% to 78.4% against the same quarter a year earlier - the company is keeping more of what it sells, not buying growth with discounts.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Operating cash flow is positive at $357.0m over the trailing year, so the business funds itself and is not dependent on raising money.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828025050698/0001628280-25-050698-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-25-050698"},{"text":"Net cash of $3.7bn against total assets of $17.1bn - no debt overhang forcing decisions.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"}],"bear":[{"text":"Growth is erratic - a standard deviation of 93.1% across 5 comparisons. Lumpy revenue usually means few customers or long contracts, and both make any single quarter a poor guide.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Diluted share count rose 8.3% over the year (Q1 2026 vs Q1 2025). The company can grow while your share of it shrinks, and this is the number most commentary ignores.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000162828026029401/0001628280-26-029401-index.htm","accession":"0001628280-26-029401"},{"text":"Officers and directors hold only 0.5% of the shares. There is little alignment between what happens to the share price and what happens to them.","source_url":"https://www.sec.gov/Archives/edgar/data/2023554/000136324926000056/0001363249-26-000056-index.htm"},{"text":"Base rate: 57.8% of US common stocks underperformed one-month Treasury bills over their lifetimes (Bessembinder, Journal of Financial Economics, 2018). Nothing above changes that starting point.","source_url":"https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jfineco.2018.06.004"}],"triggers":[{"id":"gross_margin_floor","kind":"metric","label":"Gross margin falls below 70.0% for 2 consecutive quar